      "markdownBody": "# CodeRabbit findings for PAN-2652 (PR #5060)\n\nCodeRabbit posted 3 inline finding(s). CodeRabbit is advisory: nothing waits for these,\nbut each one gets an answer, either a fix or a reply with your reason.\n\n- Thread 4486773690 · src/lib/overdeck/conversation-fork-adoption.ts:322 [Minor]: The marker-scan gate can permanently skip a fork that the first scan missed.\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5060#discussion_r4486773690\n- Thread 4486773725 · src/lib/overdeck/conversation-message.ts:481 [Major]: Return an error when the post-compact restart fails.\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5060#discussion_r4486773725\n- Thread 4486773732 · src/lib/overdeck/conversation-session-events.ts:8 [Minor]: Make session-change notifications cross-process.\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5060#discussion_r4486773732\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Read each thread (open its link, or the code at the path and line).\n2. If you agree with a finding, fix it.\n3. If you reject a finding, reply on its thread with your reason:\n   `gh api repos/eltmon/overdeck/pulls/5060/comments/<thread id>/replies -f body=\"<reason>\"`\n4. If you changed code: run the quality gates on what you touched, commit, push, then run `pan review request PAN-2652`.\n   If you only replied, you are done.\n5. If PR #5060 has already merged when you read this, nothing more lands on it: open a follow-up issue\n   for the findings you agree with instead of pushing."
